From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:26:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: keep the boot crumbs where a watchdog
 reset leaves them

The boot-crumb record at 0xf818 does not survive the resets it is meant
to explain. After the first watchdog reset on a kernel that writes it,
the next boot found no record and printed nothing, and across a macOS
round trip a test pattern there came back with 0xf818 (the magic) and
0xf81b cleared. In the same runs the bytes at 0xf810-0xf816 kept their
pattern across a watchdog reset and a normal reboot.

Move the record to 0xf810 and drop its trailing zero byte, which nothing
reads: magic, the entered/left mask, the heartbeat and the last external
DCP power step fit in seven bytes, ending before 0xf817, which belongs
to someone else.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 9 +++++----
 drivers/soc/apple/boot-crumb.c                | 6 +++---
 include/linux/soc/apple/boot-crumb.h          | 4 ++--
 3 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index e08093a8c0..44395ae198 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -206,11 +206,12 @@ resume_exception: resume-exception@f804 {
 				};
 				/*
 				 * Boot crumbs: early sections entered and not left, heartbeat, the
-				 * last external-DCP power step. Free bytes of the legacy scratch,
-				 * which is backed at 0xf800-0xf82f only.
+				 * last external-DCP power step. Free bytes of the legacy scratch
+				 * that keep a write across a watchdog reset; 0xf818 and 0xf81b
+				 * come back cleared after one.
 				 */
-				boot_crumb: boot-crumb@f818 {
-					reg = <0xf818 0x08>;
+				boot_crumb: boot-crumb@f810 {
+					reg = <0xf810 0x07>;
 				};
 				panic_count: panic-count@f802,4 {
 					reg = <0xf802 0x01>;
diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/boot-crumb.c b/drivers/soc/apple/boot-crumb.c
index 60b6a8487e..a7f7390910 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/boot-crumb.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/boot-crumb.c
@@ -13,9 +13,9 @@
  *
  * Record (APPLE_CRUMB_RECORD_LEN bytes): magic, a little-endian u32 mask with
  * bit 2n = section n entered and bit 2n + 1 = section n left, the heartbeat
- * second (APPLE_CRUMB_BEAT_DONE once the window passed), the last external
- * DCP power step (section << 4 | step, see apple_crumb_steps) and a zero. A clean
- * shutdown clears it. Nothing is written after the window.
+ * second (APPLE_CRUMB_BEAT_DONE once the window passed) and the last external
+ * DCP power step (section << 4 | step, see apple_crumb_steps). A clean shutdown
+ * clears it. Nothing is written after the window.
  */
 
 #include <linux/atomic.h>
diff --git a/include/linux/soc/apple/boot-crumb.h b/include/linux/soc/apple/boot-crumb.h
index 5c74305004..d0b67cb012 100644
--- a/include/linux/soc/apple/boot-crumb.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/apple/boot-crumb.h
@@ -30,8 +30,8 @@ enum apple_boot_crumb {
 	APPLE_CRUMB_COUNT
 };
 
-/* The PMU scratch record: magic, entered/left mask (le32), heartbeat, dcpext step, 0. */
-#define APPLE_CRUMB_RECORD_LEN	8
+/* The PMU scratch record: magic, entered/left mask (le32), heartbeat, dcpext step. */
+#define APPLE_CRUMB_RECORD_LEN	7
 
 /* Writes the record to the PMU; may sleep. Registered by macsmc-reboot. */
 typedef int (*apple_boot_crumb_writer_t)(void *ctx, const u8 *rec, size_t len);
-- 
2.43.0

